Materials and supplies for a small business are defined as tangible property that is used or consumed in the taxpayer's operations and is not inventory. This includes items that are:
(i) Components acquired to maintain, repair, or improve a unit of tangible property not acquired as part of any single unit of property;
(ii) Fuel, lubricants, water, and similar items expected to be consumed within 12 months or less;
(iii) Units of property with an economic useful life of 12 months or less;
(iv) Units of property with an acquisition or production cost of $200 or less; or
(v) Items identified in published guidance as materials and supplies permitted under this section [26 CFR 1.162-3(c)(1)].
